• I fixed the call-merging/control-flow bugs in builder.go and call_inline.go.

  The main fixes were:

  - merged-call continuations now keep the caller CFG valid instead of returning out of the parent process
  - internal callee builds no longer reuse stale process/SSA state across call sites
  - phi predecessor edges are retargeted when a block is split at a call, so loop-carried values actually update
  - process edge rebuilding/order now stays consistent after inlining

